{"id":"1da3f204-a593-44fa-b52a-f67c7f543633","object":"chat.completion","created":1784882919,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    wt_indices = case.get('word_token_indices')\\n    w_labels = case.get('word_labels')\\n    token_count = case.get('token_count')\\n    if not isinstance(wt_indices, list) or not isinstance(w_labels, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"word_token_indices and word_labels must be lists\\\")\\n    if len(wt_indices) != len(w_labels):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"word_token_indices and word_labels length mismatch\\\")\\n    all_tokens = set()\\n    for group in wt_indices:\\n        if not isinstance(group, list):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Each group must be a list\\\")\\n        for t in group:\\n            if not isinstance(t, int) or t < 0 or t >= token_count:\\n                raise ValueError(\\\"Invalid token index\\\")\\n            if t in all_tokens:\\n                raise ValueError(\\\"Overlapping token indices\\\")\\n            all_tokens.add(t)\\n    if len(all_tokens) != token_count:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Uncovered token indices (missing or extra)\\\")\\n    token_labels = [0] * token_count\\n    for group, label in zip(wt_indices, w_labels):\\n        for t in group:\\n            token_labels[t] = label\\n    kept_indices = [i for i, lbl in enumerate(token_labels) if lbl == 1]\\n    return {\\n        \\\"kept_indices\\\": kept_indices,\\n        \\\"token_labels\\\": token_labels\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to generate a Python implementation for solve(case) that takes a payload with word_token_indices (list of lists of ints), word_labels (list of ints), token_count (int). It should project word-level labels onto subword tokens. For each word group (list of token indices), assign the word label to each token. Then, create a list of token labels of length token_count, initialized maybe to -1 or something, but we need to ensure every token index from 0 to token_count-1 is covered exactly once? Actually problem says \"Reject overlapping, out-of-range, or uncovered token indices.\" So we must verify that the union of all token indices across all word groups is exactly the set {0,...,token_count-1}, with no overlaps and no missing. Then produce token_labels (list of ints of length token_count, each token's label). Then kept_indices are the token indices where token_labels == 1.\n\nThe required output: { \"kept_indices\": [int], \"token_labels\": [int] }.\n\nWe must raise ValueError if invalid.\n\nImplementation steps:\n- Validate that word_token_indices is a list, non-empty? Possibly not required but from examples it has items. word_labels same length.\n- Collect all token indices from all groups, check for duplicates (overlap) and out-of-range (>= token_count or <0). Also check that every token from 0 to token_count-1 appears exactly once. Use set and list.\n- After validation, construct token_labels array of length token_count, fill with label from corresponding word group. Since each token appears in exactly one group, we can iterate over groups.\n- Then compute kept_indices = [i for i, label in enumerate(token_labels) if label == 1].\n- Return dict with kept_indices and token_labels.\n\nNote: The output schema requires that token_labels be an array of integers. kept_indices sorted? Not specified but typically kept_indices should be in increasing order. We'll assume sorted.\n\nAlso consider: The payload may have _case_nonce but we ignore.\n\nImplementation as a function solve(case) that returns dict.\n\nNow, produce the JSON output with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a JSON string.\n\nMake sure to escape properly: backslashes, quotes, newlines.\n\nI'll write the Python code carefully.\n\nLet me write solve(case):\n\ndef solve(case):\n    # Extract fields\n    wt_indices = case.get('word_token_indices')\n    w_labels = case.get('word_labels')\n    token_count = case.get('token_count')\n    if not isinstance(wt_indices, list) or not isinstance(w_labels, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"word_token_indices and word_labels must be lists\")\n    if len(wt_indices) != len(w_labels):\n        raise ValueError(\"word_token_indices and word_labels length mismatch\")\n    # Validate token indices\n    all_tokens = set()\n    for group in wt_indices:\n        if not isinstance(group, list):\n            raise ValueError(\"Each group must be a list\")\n        for t in group:\n            if not isinstance(t, int) or t < 0 or t >= token_count:\n                raise ValueError(\"Invalid token index\")\n            if t in all_tokens:\n                raise ValueError(\"Overlapping token indices\")\n            all_tokens.add(t)\n    # Check coverage\n    if len(all_tokens) != token_count:\n        raise ValueError(\"Uncovered token indices (missing or extra)\")\n    # Build token_labels\n    token_labels = [0] * token_count\n    for group, label in zip(wt_indices, w_labels):\n        for t in group:\n            token_labels[t] = label\n    # Compute kept_indices\n    kept_indices = [i for i, lbl in enumerate(token_labels) if lbl == 1]\n    return {\n        \"kept_indices\": kept_indices,\n        \"token_labels\": token_labels\n    }\n\nThat's it.\n\nNow produce JSON.\n\nI need to wrap the Python code as a string inside a JSON object with key \"implementation\". Ensure proper escaping.\n\nI'll write the code string with newlines as \\n, double quotes as \\\", etc.\n\nLet me do it step by step."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1239,"completion_tokens":1240,"total_tokens":2479,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":884},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":1239},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}